<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to use privatization revs to cut debt only.</title>
<headline>Brazil to use privatization revs to cut debt only.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil will continue to use revenues from its privatization program to reduce its debt stockpile, Finance Minister Pedro Malan said Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Privatization revenues are only for retiring public debt,&quot; Malan told reporters at a news conference to unveil a packet of measures to cut spending and increase revenues.</p>
<p>The possibility of privatization cash being used for infrastructure projects was raised to smooth resistance in Congress to the 1997 privatization of mining giant Companhia Vale do Rio Doce (CVRD). The bill was subsequently scrapped.</p>
<p>-- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358</p>
